# Copy this file to .env for local development. NEVER commit the real
# .env file — it is already excluded in .gitignore.
#
# This app uses a self-hosted local language model, not a third-party
# hosted-AI provider — there is no API key for OpenAI/Anthropic/etc.
# anywhere in this project. See ../README.md for the full architecture.

# Where your self-hosted inference server's OpenAI-compatible API lives.
# For local development against a llama.cpp server running on this same
# machine:
LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/v1
# For local development against Ollama instead:
#LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/v1

# Never hard-coded into application logic — change this to benchmark or
# run a different model without touching any code.
LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=qwen3:4b

# Optional. Most local llama.cpp/Ollama setups need no key at all. Set
# this only if you've put your own auth in front of your inference
# server. This is a credential for YOUR OWN infrastructure, never a
# third-party provider key.
#LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=

# Uncomment and set to "production" when deploying for real. In
# production mode, the server refuses to start if LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL is
# a localhost/127.0.0.1 address — see lib/config.ts.
#NODE_ENV=production

#PORT=3000
